hadiths[33]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2872","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) said: ""There is a tree in Paradise, under whose shade a rider walks for a hundred years, even then he will not be able to cross it. If you wish, recite: ""Wazil al-Mamdud"" (Al-Waqa'ah: 30/56) meaning there are long shadows in Paradise."""
"2873","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) heard from the Prophet (PBUH), he (PBUH) said: ""There is a tree in Paradise under whose shade the rider (horse) will walk for a hundred years and yet the shade will not end. It will be the shade of the tree of Khalid. That is, a tree that remains forever."""
"2874","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Ajwa (date) is from Paradise (among the fruits) and it is an antidote for poison."""
"2875","On the authority of Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed there is a market in Paradise."" The Companions asked: What is that? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""They are two mounds of sand with the scent of musk. People will go there and gather in it, then Allah will blow a wind for them that will enter their houses (when they return) and their wives will say: Your beauty and beauty increased greatly after you left us, and they will say to their wives: You also became like this after us (i.e., your beauty and beauty became more refined)."""
"2876","There is a hadith similar to the above-mentioned hadith from this document."
"2877","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Paradise is surrounded by things that are repulsive to the soul, and hell is surrounded by the desires of the soul."""
"2878","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I was sitting in the (Prophet's) mosque and the poor among the emigrants were sitting in a circle when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and sat next to them. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) said: I saw that their faces were shining until I began to wish that I too could be one of them."
"2879","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Hell complained before its Lord and said: 'O my Lord! Some of me have eaten others, so Allah Ta'ala has allowed it two breaths, one breath in the cold (season) and one in the heat, so what you experience extreme heat and extreme cold is because of this Zamhir."""
"2880","From this chain of narrators, Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrated the same."
"2881","Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: ""This (worldly) fire of yours is one-seventieth (in its heat and lethality) of the fire of Hell."""
"2882","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The lightest punishment (in Hell) will be the one who wears two shoes that open his mind (like hot water)."""
"2883","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The people of Hell will be thrown into Hell, and they will say: ""Is there more?"" Is there anything else? Are there any others? She will say three times until Allah Almighty places His blessed foot on her, then she will shrink and say: Enough, enough, enough."
"2884","Ameerul Momineen Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) said: Learn the duties, the rules, and the Sunan, just as you learn the Qur'an."
"2885","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Learn the knowledge of duties because it is part of your religion."
"2886","Ibn Shihab Al-Zuhari, may Allah have mercy on him, said: If Uthman and Zayd died at some point, the knowledge of duties would cease, and there came a time when no one knew the knowledge of duties except these two."
"2887","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may God be pleased with him) said: Learn the Holy Qur'an and knowledge of the duties, it is possible that a person will need such knowledge that he knew or it will reach people who do not know it (the duties)."
"2888","Abu Musa said: The example of the one who acquired knowledge of the Qur'an and did not learn the duties is like a head without a face. (In one version it is «Maslah al-Muslim al-Brans») Its example is like a dress in which there is a cap and no face)."
"2889","Ibrahim Nakhai said: I said to Alqamah: I do not understand what to ask you? He said: Kill your neighbor."
"2890","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Learn the rules of duties, divorce and Hajj because these are from your religion."
"2891","Hasan al-Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The righteous Salaf used to encourage learning the Holy Qur’an, knowledge of duties, and rituals (members of Hajj worship)."
"2892","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: He who has read the Qur'an should learn the knowledge of duty because if a villager meets him and says: O emigrant (brother)! Do you read Quran? If he said: Yes, I read, then he will say: Can you divide the inheritance? If he said yes I can, then this is more knowledge and improvement, and if he said: I do not know Ilm al-Fareez, then the Arab will say: Then what is the difference between me and you, O migrant brother. (That is, I am also ignorant of knowledge and duties and you are also ignorant of it)."
"2893","Muslim said: We asked Masrooq: Did Umm al-Momineen Sayyidah Aisha (RA) know the duties well? He said: By the One besides whom there is no god, I saw the great companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that they also used to ask him about their duties."
"2894","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Saad bin Abi Waqqas and Sayyidna Abu Bakrah, may Allah be pleased with them, that Shuba said, and Sayyidna Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him, was the one who first shot an arrow in the way of Allah, and Sayyidna Abu Bakrah, may God be pleased with him, was the one who climbed the fort of Taif and came down to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. Knowing that he is not her father, then heaven is forbidden to him.”"
"2895","Sayyiduna Abu Bakr al-Sadiq (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Claiming an unknown lineage is disbelief against Allah, similarly, claiming innocence from any lineage, even if it is just a little, is disbelief against Allah."
"2896","It is narrated from this chain of narrators on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) in the same manner as mentioned above."
"2897","Qays bin Abi Hazim said: I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to swear allegiance to him, but when he reached (Madinah), he (may God bless him and grant him peace) had passed away and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may God be pleased with him) was his vicegerent (Khalifa), so he praised him a lot and wept a lot and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: “To deny even the slightest lineage is disbelief with Allah.” is, and to claim an unknown (unknown) lineage is also disbelief with Allah.”"
"2898","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever claims to be the father of someone else instead of his father, or makes his mooli (liberator) someone other than those who freed him, then the curse of Allah, the angels of Allah, and all people will be upon him until the Day of Resurrection, and none of his deeds or wealth will be acceptable."""
"2899","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: When Sayyidna Umar (RA) was with us on a journey, we found it easy. He said about the share of the husband and parents that the husband will get half and the mother will get a third of the remaining wealth."
"2900","Yazid al-Rishk said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayb, may God have mercy on him: When a man leaves behind his wife and parents, how will the inheritance be divided? He said: Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) divided it among four."
"2901","Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (RA) said in the issue of wife and parents: The wife will get a quarter and the mother will get a third of what is left."
"2902","Sayyiduna Uthman ibn Affan (may God be pleased with him) said: The wife's share will be one-fourth of the four, and what is left of the four for the mother will be one-third and one-third, and the father's share will be two-thirds (i.e. two-thirds)."
"2903","Umar bin Saeed asked Harith Al-Awur about the inheritance of his wife and parents, so he explained the (above) problem of Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2904","Sayyiduna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) said about a woman who leaves her husband and parents, the husband will get half of what is left, and the mother will get a third of what is left."
